                                "sense_id": "b61a7b53-be1b-3f69-a2b3-ea936d069d6e",
                                "text": "From this trunk, like a tower, rose an enormous tenfold ramification, the branches of which crossed and intercrossed, and forked and developed, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "442bc57f-3635-3eed-a85b-5f40dab870bd",
                        "entry_id": "1f8658bc-6f33-3384-8430-d485eba7d6fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To breed two strains having a common ancestry with one another"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4165522c-cf7a-4910-97cf-cd25cf39cc6c",
                                "sense_id": "442bc57f-3635-3eed-a85b-5f40dab870bd",
                                "text": "A species varies occasionally in two directions, but owing to their free intercrossing they (the variations) never increase."
                            }
                        ]
